Package: FullLokalRFFA
Type: Package
Title: Full Local and Regional Flood Frequency Analysis in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emmanuel", "Jjunju", email = "your.email@nve.no", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Trond", "Reitan", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Expands upon original R scripts developed by Trond Reitan (2025) 
    for conducting Full Local and Regional Flood Frequency Analysis (RFFA), 
    implementing the methodology described in NVE Report 10/2020 
    <https://publikasjoner.nve.no/rapport/2020/rapport2020_10.pdf> by Engeland 
    et al. (2020). Provides an alternative to NVE's Hydra2 flood analysis 
    tool by combining Trond's core MCMC and regional analysis logic with 
    custom supporting functions built by Emmanuel Jjunju (NVE) for streamlined 
    data import (from Sildre, NEVINA shapefiles, etc.), processing, and plotting. 
    Enables users to run Bayesian MCMC parameter estimation, Generalized Extreme 
    Value (GEV) calculations, return-period plots, and quantile tables directly 
    within R. Note that this method is designed for daily flood data (ideally 
    catchments > 60 km² with 10–25+ years of records) and is not intended for 
    instantaneous or hourly peak flow (findata) analysis. This package is 
    provided as-is for research and supplementary use at the user's own risk; 
    users should always refer to officially published NVE tools and guidelines 
    for authoritative flood frequency analyses.
